    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65754" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεῖραξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰκος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>young girl, lass</i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				187
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				301
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				410
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ec.</u>
				611
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1071
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1079
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Xenarch.
				4.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Pk.</u>
				14
			</span></i>: used as fem. of men, <i>qui muliebria patiuntur</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				5
			</span></i>: in later writers masc., <i>boy, lad</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				1.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				4.19
			</span></i>. (Cf. Skt. <i>maryakás</i> 'manikin',
				<i>máryas</i> 'young man'.)</div>
